  "verdict": "H4: NO genuinely-new beat-32B slice (inside an always-32B dataset) is robust: across 8 splits the mean BH-FDR5 survivor count is 0.25 and the mean raw genuinely-new count (1.62) sits BELOW the label-permutation null (mean 5.61, p95 15); no new slice recurs in more than 5/8 splits (closest near-miss: MedXpertQA-MM|bsys=Respiratory certified in 5/8 splits).  Discovery instead reliably RE-FINDS the known PMC/MMMU wins as echoes (validates the F1 hand-gate).  The beat does NOT extend past PMC/MMMU via slice structure -> 6th independent confirmation of the recoverability wall (the honest deliverable).  H8: naive point routing overfits thin slices (7.5 held-out violations/split, fine family, 8 splits) -- the overfit risk is REAL.  Buhlmann credibility shrinkage helps only MARGINALLY (7.5->6.62) and is DOMINATED by the simple CI lower-bound guardrail F1 already deploys (7.5->0.25 at preserved beat +0.0117).  So the routing is made guardrail-honest by F1's existing CI-guardrail, NOT by the fancier actuarial estimator; H8's value is diagnostic (confirms overfit + validates the guardrail).  H2: kNN neighborhood-recovery beats the scalar margin gate on 0/5 MCQ datasets -> no consistent MCQ gain; the escalation signal is intrinsically weak on MCQ (recoverability wall)."
